gfs2: Get rid of gfs2_log_[un]lock helpers

jira KERNEL-878
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-4.18.0-553.120.1.el8_10
commit-author Andreas Gruenbacher <agruenba@redhat.com>
commit 5a15907f99e5d93b0133be608a9bbe24fd76f67a
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-4.18.0-553.120.1.el8_10/5a15907f.failed

These two helpers only hide the locking operation; they do not make
the code more readable.

Created with:

sed -i -e 's:gfs2_log_unlock(sdp):spin_unlock(\&sdp->sd_log_lock):' \
       -e 's:gfs2_log_lock(sdp):spin_lock(\&sdp->sd_log_lock):'

	Signed-off-by: Andreas Gruenbacher <agruenba@redhat.com>
(cherry picked from commit 5a15907f99e5d93b0133be608a9bbe24fd76f67a)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	fs/gfs2/aops.c
#	fs/gfs2/glops.c
#	fs/gfs2/trans.c
diff --cc fs/gfs2/aops.c
index 3283c12712d0,403b5e1fada4..000000000000
--- a/fs/gfs2/aops.c
+++ b/fs/gfs2/aops.c
@@@ -708,21 -652,23 +708,26 @@@ int gfs2_releasepage(struct page *page
  	struct buffer_head *bh, *head;
  	struct gfs2_bufdata *bd;
  
 -	head = folio_buffers(folio);
 -	if (!head)
 -		return false;
 +	if (!page_has_buffers(page))
 +		return 0;
  
  	/*
 -	 * mm accommodates an old ext3 case where clean folios might
 -	 * not have had the dirty bit cleared.	Thus, it can send actual
 -	 * dirty folios to ->release_folio() via shrink_active_list().
 +	 * From xfs_vm_releasepage: mm accommodates an old ext3 case where
 +	 * clean pages might not have had the dirty bit cleared.  Thus, it can
 +	 * send actual dirty pages to ->releasepage() via shrink_active_list().
  	 *
 -	 * As a workaround, we skip folios that contain dirty buffers
 -	 * below.  Once ->release_folio isn't called on dirty folios
 -	 * anymore, we can warn on dirty buffers like we used to here
 -	 * again.
 +	 * As a workaround, we skip pages that contain dirty buffers below.
 +	 * Once ->releasepage isn't called on dirty pages anymore, we can warn
 +	 * on dirty buffers like we used to here again.
  	 */
  
++<<<<<<< HEAD
 +	gfs2_log_lock(sdp);
 +	head = bh = page_buffers(page);
++=======
+ 	spin_lock(&sdp->sd_log_lock);
+ 	bh = head;
++>>>>>>> 5a15907f99e5 (gfs2: Get rid of gfs2_log_[un]lock helpers)
  	do {
  		if (atomic_read(&bh->b_count))
  			goto cannot_release;
@@@ -753,13 -699,13 +758,18 @@@
  
  		bh = bh->b_this_page;
  	} while (bh != head);
- 	gfs2_log_unlock(sdp);
+ 	spin_unlock(&sdp->sd_log_lock);
  
 -	return try_to_free_buffers(folio);
 +	return try_to_free_buffers(page);
  
  cannot_release:
++<<<<<<< HEAD
 +	gfs2_log_unlock(sdp);
 +	return 0;
++=======
+ 	spin_unlock(&sdp->sd_log_lock);
+ 	return false;
++>>>>>>> 5a15907f99e5 (gfs2: Get rid of gfs2_log_[un]lock helpers)
  }
  
  static const struct address_space_operations gfs2_aops = {
